            <ArticleTitle>Medicare Pays for Chronic Care Management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As of January, the Centers for Medicare &amp;amp; Medicaid Services began paying for chronic care management of patients with two or more conditions under its Chronic Care Management program. The payment applies to patients in traditional fee-for-service and noncapitated Medicare Advantage plan arrangements. Texas Medical Association leaders caution the program has some hefty requirements.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
